gfxboot keel notes
==================

The ISO of a Keel appliance boots into the cdroot gfxboot-keel
(CDROOT ?= gfxboot-keel in mk/turnkey.mk of Keel-Linux/common). It is a
copy of gfxboot-turnkey with one change: splash.pcx, the background image
of the boot menu, shows the Keel mark and the "KEEL LINUX" wordmark. The
theme code (bootlogo, en.tr) is the same as in gfxboot-turnkey.
gfxboot-turnkey stays as it is, so that the diffs to upstream stay clear.

- gfxboot-keel/isolinux

    - bootlogo      # packed archive of src/gfxboot-keel-bootlogo

- src/gfxboot-keel-bootlogo

    - splash.pcx    # 640x480, PCX, 8-bit colour; made by src/keel-splash
    - all other files are copies of src/gfxboot-turnkey-bootlogo

- src/keel-splash   # not in the archive

    - keel-mark-dark.svg    # the Keel mark for a dark background
                            # (keellinux.org/assets/keel-mark-dark.svg)
    - make-splash.sh        # makes splash.pcx from keel-mark-dark.svg

To change the Keel boot menu image:

    apt-get install gfxboot librsvg2-bin imagemagick fonts-dejavu-core

    src/keel-splash/make-splash.sh
    cd src
    gfxboot --archive gfxboot-keel-bootlogo \
        --pack-archive ../gfxboot-keel/isolinux/bootlogo
    cd ..
    bats tests/

Do not put other files in src/gfxboot-keel-bootlogo: --pack-archive packs
all the files of the directory. tests/gfxboot-keel.bats unpacks the archive
again and compares each file with its source.

To see the menu without a full build, make an ISO of the cdroot with the
syslinux modules that fab copies in (cdroot-dynamic in fab's product.mk:
isolinux.bin, ldlinux, libcom32, vesamenu, gfxboot and chain .c32 from
the syslinux and isolinux packages) and boot it with qemu-system-x86_64
-cdrom. No kernel is necessary to see the menu.

The ISO boots with BIOS (isolinux) only. fab's product.iso target uses
run-genisoimage, not run-genisoimage-uefi, and this repository has no
efi.img (UEFI boot support was rolled back upstream).


gfxboot turnkey notes
=====================

- gfxboot-turnkey/isolinux

    - bootlogo      # packed archive of src/gfxboot-turnkey-bootlogo

- src/gfxboot-turnkey-bootlogo

    - en.tr         # tweaked and compiled gfxboot-theme-ubuntu
    - bootlogo      # tweaked and compiled gfxboot-theme-ubuntu

    gfxboot --archive gfxboot-turnkey-bootlogo --pack-archive bootlogo

- gfxboot-theme-ubuntu

    apt-get install gfxboot gfxboot-dev make xz-utils wget
    wget ..../gfxboot-theme-ubuntu...., unpack

    cd gfxboot-theme-ubuntu
    rm po/*.po

    - tweak panel.inc           # see below
    - tweak dia_fulloptions.inc # see below

    make
    copy out install/{bootlogo, en.tr}


